NOABOP — RAILWAY

FILES:
- index.js
- deploy-commands.js
- config.js
- package.json

ENVIRONMENT VARIABLE:
TOKEN=your_bot_token

VOLUME:
Mount Path: /app/data

START COMMAND:
npm run deploy && npm start

DISCORD DEVELOPER PORTAL -> BOT -> PRIVILEGED GATEWAY INTENTS:
- SERVER MEMBERS INTENT: ON
- MESSAGE CONTENT INTENT: ON

RECOMMENDED BOT PERMISSIONS:
- View Channels
- Send Messages
- Embed Links
- Attach Files
- Read Message History
- Manage Channels
- Manage Roles
- Manage Messages

IMPORTANT:
The NoaBop managed role must be ABOVE:
- Chat Mute role
- all roles listed in takeRoleIds

TAKE ROLE:
Run /setup-take-role.
The button label is fetched automatically from each Discord role name.

TICKETS:
Run /ticket-panel.

STAFF APPLICATION:
Run /staff-panel.

STAFF STATS:
!stats
!stats @member
Only Staff can use it.
Shows Voice Time, Messages, Helps Taken, Tickets Taken and average claim/response times.
It DOES NOT show roles, warns, removals, kicks/bans, etc.

HELP CENTER:
!h

MODERATION:
Only /chatmute is included.


GRAPHIC PANELS:
- !h now creates a graphical Help Center card with the server image in the background.
- /ticket-panel creates a graphical support panel with the server image in the background.
- /staff-panel creates a graphical staff recruitment panel with only Apply For Staff below it.
- panelBackgroundUrl is optional. If empty, the bot uses the Server Banner and then the Server Icon.

VERIFY:
- Put the Member role ID in memberRoleId.
- Run /verify-panel.
- Users click Verify and instantly receive Member.
- There is NO number challenge.
- Verify does NOT change channel permissions.
